            <title>[LU-20215] lfs mirror extend -N=&lt;NUMBER-OF-MIRRORS&gt; to return error status</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20215</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When lfs mirror extend -N=&amp;lt;number of mirrors&amp;gt; is issued with wrong number of mirrors and rejected, it does not return error status. It is required in hotpools when we need to know that the command was rejected. The purpose:  1) to prevent the consequent lfs setstripe --comp-set --comp-flags=prefer 2) for statistics.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Currently I see the command returns the status 0&lt;/p&gt;</description>
